# Frozen terrain fill-face verdicts — the reviewed output of the fill-tag
# sweep (scripts/terrain-fill-sweep.sh; measurement provenance per line).
# verdict level sector face need-px provenance
#
# FILL   = og draws this LP surface over sightlines no authored HP covers
#          (water planes, level-boundary channels); the fill pass may draw it.
# NOFILL = the need is a silhouette sliver between the coarse/alternate LP
#          shape and the HP silhouette (or an island-rim fringe); filling
#          paints LP wedges over sky around detailed HP. Reviewed 2026-08-05;
#          the haunted lp-bridge cluster is NOFILL by review (the HP bridge
#          alone reads correctly at distance).
#
# Two sanctioned ways to reach this file, both ending in a reviewed verdict:
#   1. the coverage sweep (scripts/terrain-fill-sweep.sh) + a per-face strip
#      review — the origin of every measured need-px row below;
#   2. the in-game inspector (P key, notes/plans/openpete-fill-tag-inspector.md):
#      aim at a face, read its identity and whether authored HP covers that
#      sightline, flip the verdict live, then fold the session file in with
#      scripts/fill-tags-apply.py. Rows it adds carry provenance `pick` and
#      need-px 0 — judged against the live scene, not a pixel measurement.
# NEVER hand-edit a FILL in without one of those. A sweep face absent here is
# unreviewed — new candidates fail loud.
